<BaseLayout title="About WasmStore" description="Learn how WasmStore organizes browser game projects, demo links, community ports, and practical gaming resources." path="/about">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">OUR APPROACH</div><h1>Built for <span class="gradient-text">game discovery</span></h1><p>A clear, useful directory for people exploring games that run in a browser.</p></div></section>
  <article class="prose wrap"><h2>What is WasmStore?</h2><p>WasmStore is an independent discovery portal for browser-playable games, community ports, web technology, and practical gaming guides. The directory brings titles, demos, and source repositories into one place so players can decide what to explore next.</p><h2>How the catalog works</h2><p>Our initial catalog is derived from the community-maintained Ultimate Catalog of Web Game Ports. Listings are discovery records: a demo link does not guarantee current availability, iframe compatibility, or permission to redistribute a game's files. Source links point readers toward upstream projects where they can check requirements and licenses.</p><h2>What we aim to do well</h2><ul><li>Label demo links and source repositories separately.</li><li>Provide a dedicated detail page with instructions, controls, and credits for each listing.</li><li>Publish practical guidance about compatibility, performance, privacy, and touch input.</li><li>Make broken links and attribution corrections easy to report.</li></ul><h2>Rights and attribution</h2><p>Game titles, trademarks, artwork, music, and other game assets belong to their respective rights holders. WasmStore does not claim ownership of third-party projects. We do not redistribute game binaries in this directory; any future self-hosted build must pass license and rights review first.</p><h2>Independence</h2><p>WasmStore is not affiliated with or endorsed by the creators or publishers of listed games unless a page explicitly says otherwise.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For corrections, suggestions, accessibility feedback, or rights concerns, use the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.</p></article>
</BaseLayout>